# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# Everything not excluded here is uploaded to the daemon on every build and,
# because the Dockerfile does `COPY ui/ ./`, ends up inside an intermediate
# image layer. In this tree ui/node_modules (~800 MB) plus ui/.next (~300 MB)
# alone are about a gigabyte of host-built artefacts that the image must not
# contain: node_modules would silently shadow the `npm ci` install, and a stale
# host .next would be overwritten by `npm run build` but still be paid for in
# upload time and layer size.
#
# Rule of thumb when editing: the build only needs server/ (Go sources +
# go.mod/go.sum), ui/ minus its generated output, and entrypoint.sh.

# --- Version control / CI ---------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.gitmodules
.github

# --- Node / Next.js generated output ----------------------------------------
# `npm ci` recreates node_modules inside the image; `npm run build` recreates
# .next. Both must come from the image, never from the host.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/.swc
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/npm-debug.log*
**/.eslintcache
**/coverage
**/.vitest

# --- Environment files ------------------------------------------------------
# No stage reads a .env, and shipping one would bake host-local (possibly
# secret) values into a layer. The one build-time value the frontend needs,
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE, is a --build-arg instead; see the Dockerfile.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# --- Go / build output ------------------------------------------------------
bin
server/bin
**/*.exe
**/*.test
**/*.out

# --- Local databases and runtime data ---------------------------------------
# /data is a bind mount at runtime; a host copy must never be baked in.
data
**/*.db
**/*.db-journal
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3

# --- Python helper scripts (repo tooling, not part of the image) ------------
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
*.py
pyproject.toml

# --- Docs, agent config and repo metadata -----------------------------------
docs
skills
*.md
LICENSE
Makefile

# --- Docker's own files -----------------------------------------------------
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.*.yml

# --- Editor / OS junk -------------------------------------------------------
.idea
.vscode
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/*.swp
**/*.swo
